# Testing Rules

- Tests must be deterministic, isolated, and safe to run offline.
- Use synthetic merchants, transaction IDs, comments, amounts, and tokens.
- Never copy personal `.env`, API payloads, reports, or transaction data into
  fixtures or snapshots.
- Freeze or inject time for date-sensitive behavior.
- Fake Monobank and rate providers at their interfaces; do not patch deep
  implementation details when dependency injection is available.
- Cover boundary behavior: inclusive dates, Kyiv timezone transitions, holds,
  duplicate authorizations, unknown MCC, currencies, empty reports, and
  upstream errors.
- API tests assert status, stable error code, response schema, and secret
  absence.
- Frontend tests assert user-visible behavior rather than implementation state.
- Keep one small end-to-end smoke path; prefer unit/integration tests for edge
  cases.
- A bug fix requires a regression test that fails before the fix.
